      "summary": "The land was part of the homeland of the Lenape people. During the Battle of Long Island in 1776, fighting took place in and around what is now the park."
    },
    {
      "period": "1850s–1860s",
      "summary": "As Brooklyn grew, civic leaders sought a large public park. An initial plan by Egbert Viele was set aside, and Frederick Law Olmsted and Calvert Vaux—designers of Manhattan's Central Park—developed a new plan."
    },
    {
      "period": "1867–1870s",
